The HTML dump code of UnNetHack has been extended to map the IBMgraphics
resp. DECgraphics characters to Unicode codepoints and dump those as
HTML entities.

That means that (as Unicode contains all the characters from the IBM-
and DECgraphics' character sets) the dumps now look much more like the
terminal output at the moment of your character's death.

If the font of your terminal is the same as the monospace font of your
browser you shouldn't even really note a difference between game screen
and the HTML dump.

Here are three example dumps of the same situation to compare the HTML
output side-by-side.

A dump using plain ASCII:
http://bhaak.dyndns.org/nethack/unnethack_dump_ascii.html
(that's how all dumps looked up until now), a dump using IBMgraphics:
http://bhaak.dyndns.org/nethack/unnethack_dump_ibm.html
and one using DECgraphics:
http://bhaak.dyndns.org/nethack/unnethack_dump_dec.html

The plain text dumps are still ASCII-only.

